# `D-32` (Dave, 2026-08-15): nothing is committed to `examples/` as data — no
# store file, no seed artifact, no fixture data. The deployment a client
# reaches is ALREADY POPULATED, and populating one is producer-side work that
# happens before a client exists.
#
# These two are what a populated deployment leaves on disk. They are named
# here so that a developer who has populated one cannot commit it by accident,
# which is the difference between a rule and a mechanism.
graph.sqlite3
graph.sqlite3-*
artifact-store/
